# AURA — Alpaca credentials (CRYPTO account, PAPER trading)
#
# This repository trades ONLY crypto symbols (BTC/USD, ETH/USD) via Alpaca —
# see SYMBOLS in aura_v05312_market_state_engine.py through
# aura_v05323_execution_specification_builder.py. Use your Alpaca CRYPTO
# account's PAPER key pair here, not your separate stocks-account keys;
# nothing in this codebase currently reads a stocks-specific credential.
#
# The codebase is not fully consistent about which env var names it reads
# (older research/backtesting scripts vs. the v0.5.3.21/.22 chain use
# different names for the same credential pair) — see
# docs/AURA_V0531622_EXECUTION_SPECIFICATION_BRIDGE_2026-09-02.md for the
# full breakdown. Set BOTH pairs below to the SAME paper key/secret so
# nothing silently falls back to a missing value.
#
# Never commit a real .env. This file is the template only — copy it to
# .env (already gitignored) and fill in real values there:
#   cp .env.example .env

# Read by: most v0.4.x research/backtesting scripts (aura_v048_live_paper.py,
# historical_signal_quality_scanner_*.py, aura_research.py,
# test_alpaca_connection.py, test_alpaca_market_data.py, etc.)
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=

# Read by: aura_v05321_alpaca_market_data.py (preferred name; falls back to
# ALPACA_API_KEY/ALPACA_SECRET_KEY above if unset), and
# aura_v05322_alpaca_paper_execution_adapter.py (required — no fallback).
ALPACA_PAPER_API_KEY=
ALPACA_PAPER_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional feature flag. Only needed to let
# aura_v05322_alpaca_paper_execution_adapter.py actually SUBMIT an order
# (when run with --submit-paper). Leave unset/false until you deliberately
# want paper-order submission enabled.
# AURA_ALPACA_PAPER_ORDERS_ENABLED=true
